# 基本図形編集のプロセスの文字枠で検索/置換のパネルを使う (design 11.3), for tools/ui_run.py:
# a figure of 30 small rectangles, two zigzag lines and one piece of text "ABC" (mkbig fig 30 4 1;
# the text 210,247 to 330,287 on the screen). The same is done with the desktop's figure editor and
# with the one running as a process: the text pressed twice to edit it, Ctrl+F for 検索/置換, "B"
# typed into 検索文字列, Enter for 次を検索 (the B found and picked), a letter typed over it,
# Escape, the figure saved. Record 0 comes out the same, byte for byte.
# The desktop's panel is worked in a loop of its own, so no sync is asked while it is up.
# Keys: Enter 28, Esc 29; with Ctrl (01) F 09, S 16, E 08.
# the desktop's figure editor opened by open, whatever the program object says (figproc kernel)
figproc kernel
mkbig fig 30 4 1
open big
waitwin 画用紙 600
sync 600
wait 500
dclick 215 255
sync 600
key 09 01
wait 800
text B
wait 300
shot find_kernel_panel
key 28
sync 600
text z
sync 600
shot find_kernel_replaced
key 29
sync 600
key 16 01
sync 600
sum show
keep kernel
key 08 01
sync 600
wait 500
mkbig fig 30 4 1
logmark
pfig big
expectsincein 60 figure: opened 画用紙 shapes 33
wait 500
logmark
dclick 215 255
expectsince figure: text editing begun
logmark
key 09 01
expectsince figure: find panel open
wait 300
text B
wait 300
shot find_process_panel
logmark
key 28
expectsince figure: find panel answered 10
wait 300
text z
wait 300
shot find_process_replaced
logmark
key 29
expectsince figure: text editing ended
logmark
key 16 01
expectsince figure: saved (0)
sum show
same kernel
key 08 01
expect figure: closed
